{"availability":"available","full":"kunchenguid/no-mistakes","name":"no-mistakes","description":"git push no-mistakes","category":"Other","language":"Go","stars":8800,"forks":949,"created":"2026-04-05T06:43:05Z","updated":"2026-10-09T05:16:46Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kunchenguid.github.io/no-mistakes/","topics":[],"demo":"https://kunchenguid.github.io/no-mistakes/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T05:48:12.970Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T05:48:12.970Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T05:48:12.970Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T22:54:57.214Z","stars":8756,"forks":942},{"at":"2026-10-09T05:48:12.970Z","stars":8800,"forks":949}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["no-mistakes puts a local git proxy in front of your real remote. Push to no-mistakes instead of origin, and it spins up a disposable worktree, runs an AI-driven validation pipeline, forwards the branch to the configured push target only after every check passes, and opens a clean PR automatically."],"features":["Non-blocking - the pipeline runs in an isolated worktree without disrupting your work.","Agent-agnostic - claude, codex, grok, rovodev, opencode, pi, copilot, antigravity, or cursor / devin / acp: via acpx, with ordered fallbacks; every gate requires a runnable configured pipeline agent.","Agent-native - /no-mistakes lets your coding agent do a task and gate it, or gate existing committed work: it runs the pipeline, has the pipeline apply safe fixes, and escalates the rest to you.","Human stays in charge - auto-fix or review findings, your call.","Clean PRs by default - push, open PR, watch CI, and auto-fix failures in one shot."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kunchenguid/no-mistakes/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ea609db5debe230dabbac996e7d5b4ffa9561a70a55a28799a8dee7a7cc24dd1","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T22:54:57.297Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T22:54:57.297Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,